{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install your table adapter as a dependency using your preferred package manager:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-managers"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/react-table\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/preact-table\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/octane-table\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/vue-table\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/solid-table\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/svelte-table\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/angular-table\"]],\"ember\":[[\"@tanstack/ember-table\"]],\"lit\":[[\"@tanstack/lit-table\"]],\"alpine\":[[\"@tanstack/alpine-table\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with React 18 or newer."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/preact-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Preact 10 or newer."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/octane-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Octane 0.1.21. It publishes authored TypeScript and TSRX, so your application must use Octane's compiler integration (for example, the Octane Vite plugin) to compile the package for its current target and mode."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Vue 3.2 or newer."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Solid 1.3 or newer."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Svelte 5 (it is built on runes). For Svelte 3/4 support, use TanStack Table v8."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Angular 19 or newer. The Angular adapter is built on Angular Signals."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"ember"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ember-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package is a v2 addon that works with Ember 5.8 or newer (Embroider or ember-auto-import v2). It is built on Glimmer's tracking system and supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gts"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gjs"},{"type":"text","value":" template tag components and Glint."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"lit"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/lit-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Lit 3 (3.1.3 or newer) and also requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@lit/context"},{"type":"text","value":" as a peer dependency."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"alpine"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/alpine-table"},{"type":"text","value":" package works with Alpine 3."}]}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"preact\",\"octane\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"angular\",\"ember\",\"lit\",\"alpine\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[],\"preact\":[],\"octane\":[],\"vue\":[],\"solid\":[],\"svelte\":[],\"angular\":[],\"ember\":[],\"lit\":[],\"alpine\":[]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Don't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":" package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"source code"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of all of the other adapters to see how they work."}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":["react","preact","octane","vue","solid","svelte","angular","ember","lit","alpine"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nBefore we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!\n\nInstall your table adapter as a dependency using your preferred package manager:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-managers\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/react-table\npreact: @tanstack/preact-table\noctane: @tanstack/octane-table\nvue: @tanstack/vue-table\nsolid: @tanstack/solid-table\nsvelte: @tanstack/svelte-table\nangular: @tanstack/angular-table\nember: @tanstack/ember-table\nlit: @tanstack/lit-table\nalpine: @tanstack/alpine-table\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-table` package works with React 18 or newer.\n\n# Preact\n\nThe `@tanstack/preact-table` package works with Preact 10 or newer.\n\n# Octane\n\nThe `@tanstack/octane-table` package works with Octane 0.1.21. It publishes authored TypeScript and TSRX, so your application must use Octane's compiler integration (for example, the Octane Vite plugin) to compile the package for its current target and mode.\n\n# Vue\n\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` package works with Vue 3.2 or newer.\n\n# Solid\n\nThe `@tanstack/solid-table` package works with Solid 1.3 or newer.\n\n# Svelte\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-table` package works with Svelte 5 (it is built on runes). For Svelte 3/4 support, use TanStack Table v8.\n\n# Angular\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` package works with Angular 19 or newer. The Angular adapter is built on Angular Signals.\n\n# Ember\n\nThe `@tanstack/ember-table` package is a v2 addon that works with Ember 5.8 or newer (Embroider or ember-auto-import v2). It is built on Glimmer's tracking system and supports `.gts`/`.gjs` template tag components and Glint.\n\n# Lit\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` package works with Lit 3 (3.1.3 or newer) and also requires `@lit/context` as a peer dependency.\n\n# Alpine\n\nThe `@tanstack/alpine-table` package works with Alpine 3.\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nDon't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the `@tanstack/table-core` package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the [source code](https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages) of all of the other adapters to see how they work.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Installation\n---\n\nBefore we dig in to the API, let's get you set up!\n\nInstall your table adapter as a dependency using your preferred package manager:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-managers\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/react-table\npreact: @tanstack/preact-table\noctane: @tanstack/octane-table\nvue: @tanstack/vue-table\nsolid: @tanstack/solid-table\nsvelte: @tanstack/svelte-table\nangular: @tanstack/angular-table\nember: @tanstack/ember-table\nlit: @tanstack/lit-table\nalpine: @tanstack/alpine-table\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nThe `@tanstack/react-table` package works with React 18 or newer.\n\n# Preact\n\nThe `@tanstack/preact-table` package works with Preact 10 or newer.\n\n# Octane\n\nThe `@tanstack/octane-table` package works with Octane 0.1.21. It publishes authored TypeScript and TSRX, so your application must use Octane's compiler integration (for example, the Octane Vite plugin) to compile the package for its current target and mode.\n\n# Vue\n\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` package works with Vue 3.2 or newer.\n\n# Solid\n\nThe `@tanstack/solid-table` package works with Solid 1.3 or newer.\n\n# Svelte\n\nThe `@tanstack/svelte-table` package works with Svelte 5 (it is built on runes). For Svelte 3/4 support, use TanStack Table v8.\n\n# Angular\n\nThe `@tanstack/angular-table` package works with Angular 19 or newer. The Angular adapter is built on Angular Signals.\n\n# Ember\n\nThe `@tanstack/ember-table` package is a v2 addon that works with Ember 5.8 or newer (Embroider or ember-auto-import v2). It is built on Glimmer's tracking system and supports `.gts`/`.gjs` template tag components and Glint.\n\n# Lit\n\nThe `@tanstack/lit-table` package works with Lit 3 (3.1.3 or newer) and also requires `@lit/context` as a peer dependency.\n\n# Alpine\n\nThe `@tanstack/alpine-table` package works with Alpine 3.\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nDon't see your favorite framework (or favorite version of your framework) listed? You can always just use the `@tanstack/table-core` package and build your own adapter in your own codebase. Usually, only a thin wrapper is needed to manage state and rendering for your specific framework. Browse the [source code](https://github.com/TanStack/table/tree/main/packages) of all of the other adapters to see how they work.\n"}
